  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Internews: Strengthening Rural Radio for impartial information in DRC</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xe4;rkt landsbygdsradio f&#xf6;r opartisk information i Demokratiska republiken Kongo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective from the inception of this intervention from 2019 is to promote a
more open and vibrant media sector that contributes to more responsive
and transparent institutions in the DRC.
Internews and its local partners will achieve this through the following intermediate
results:
1: Legal and regulatory environment for media is strengthened;
2: Targeted media outlets are more independent and professional;
3: Access to high-quality public-interest reporting is increased.
In addition to the above, the intervention was amended in June 2020 to also address
resistance toward COVID-19 vaccination by:
1: Strengthening health systems in DRC to face the challenge of COVID-19
2: Building trust around COVID-19 vaccines to ensure greater access and uptake
through establishing healthy information ecosystems in DRC to address mis- and
desinformation and vaccine hesitancy.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Projektet &#xe4;r utformat f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla h&#xe5;llbara politiska reformer samt digitala h&#xe5;llbara oberoende medier och civilsamh&#xe4;lle i DRK. F&#xf6;r att &#xe5;stadkomma detta beh&#xf6;vs tillr&#xe4;cklig kompetens och kunskap samt tillf&#xf6;rlitliga verktyg s&#xe5; att medborgarna erh&#xe5;ller korrekt och opartisk information. Politiska reformer, digitalt aktiverade och h&#xe5;llbara oberoende medier och civilsamh&#xe4;llet i Demokratiska republiken Kongo f&#xf6;r att ha de f&#xe4;rdigheter, kunskap och verktyg som de beh&#xf6;ver f&#xf6;r att n&#xe5; medborgarna med korrekt och opartisk information som fr&#xe4;mjar inkludering och ansvarsutkr&#xe4;vande.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is designed to ensure a resilient, policy reforms, digitally-enabled and sustainable independent media and civil society in DRC to have the skills, knowledge and tools they need to reach citizens with accurate and impartial information that promotes inclusion and accountability</narrative>
  </description>
